      "message": "`import_ubuf()` and `__import_iovec()` (as well as `process_vm_rw` in CL 4312492) keep user pointers tagged (e.g., Scudo/TBI/MTE top-byte tags in bits `[63:56]`). In the native path, `gup_fast_fallback()` and `__get_user_pages()` strip the tag via `untagged_addr()` / `untagged_addr_remote()`.\n\nHere, `start \u003d addr \u0026 PAGE_MASK_4KB` retains the top-byte tag. `p3s_gup_remote(mm, va, ...)` succeeds because `__get_user_pages()` untags `va` internally, but `p3s_slice_run_merge()` then calls `vma_lookup(mm, va)` (line 155) with the still-tagged `va`. Since `va \u003e\u003d TASK_SIZE_4KB`, `vma_lookup()` returns `NULL`, `p3s_slice_run_merge()` returns `0`, all pinned pages are released, and `p3s_get_user_slice_pages()` fails with `-EFAULT`.\n\nPlease untag `addr` at the start of `p3s_get_user_slice_pages()` (e.g., `addr \u003d untagged_addr(addr);`, or `addr \u003d untagged_addr_remote(mm, addr);` after acquiring `mmap_lock`).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "0196abdd6d2b3f548dd302efbc478868c8cccd7c",
