      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using `avail \u003d maxpages - run.nr_pages` to cap `chunk` conflates 4KB input slices with 16KB compacted host-page slots in `pages[]`. When a caller passes a pre-allocated `pages[]` array with a small `maxpages`:\n- If `maxpages \u003d\u003d 1` (e.g., `iov_iter_get_pages2(..., 1, ...)`), `avail` is 1, so `chunk \u003d 1` and the loop exits after 1 slice (4KB) because `run.nr_pages \u003d\u003d maxpages`, even when up to 4 contiguous slices (16KB) map the same 16KB host page in `pages[0]`.\n- With `maxpages \u003d\u003d 16` (`PVM_MAX_PP_ARRAY_COUNT` in `process_vm_access.c`) and a 64-slice (256KB) contiguous buffer, as `run.nr_pages` approaches 16, `avail` shrinks (`13, 9, 7, 5, 4, 3, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1`), forcing 14 separate `p3s_gup_remote()` calls (the last 5 pinning 1 slice each) and stopping with `pages[15]` only 1/4 populated (`61/64` slices).\n\nConsider using a small 4-entry stack array (`struct page *scratch[P3S_SLICES_PER_PAGE]`) when `avail \u003c P3S_SLICES_PER_PAGE` and allowing the loop to finish the remaining slices (`P3S_SLICE_MASK - run.slice`) of `run.pages[maxpages - 1]` when `run.nr_pages \u003d\u003d maxpages`.",
